      "target": "../sections/sec-001-executive-summary.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\nxecutive Summary\nE\nSeveral international agencies provided their perspectives: the World Bank, UNAIDS\nand USAID. Contributions were made by WHO regional offices (Africa, Southeast\nAsia and Western Pacific) and by WHO’s Department of HIV/AIDS/STIs.\nThere was a summary of international progress with the ProTEST initiative, the\nformal evaluation of which is still under way.\nIssues arising which were considered by the meeting to be of particular importance\nincluded:\n• the need to pull together information from all the TB/HIV projects that are \nongoing and ensure regular data coll",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Continues the executive summary with the perspectives of international agencies and WHO offices, the progress of the ProTEST initiative, and key issues raised, such as data collection, patients falling between TB and HIV programmes and adherence to preventive treatment. It reports that the draft guidelines on collaborative TB/HIV activities were endorsed subject to shortening, and introduces the main recommendations and the working group's background.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
